      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat olive oil in a large pan over medium heat. Add garlic and cook for 1 minute until fragrant."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add aubergine cubes and all spices. Stir to coat. Cook for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour in canned tomatoes and add salt. Stir and cover. Cook on medium-low heat for 20 minutes, stirring occasionally, until aubergine is completely soft."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove lid and increase heat to medium. Cook for 5 more minutes to reduce any excess liquid."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Use a fork to mash the mixture to a rough paste. Add lemon juice and most of the coriander. Taste and adjust seasoning."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Serve at room temperature, scattered with remaining coriander and a drizzle of olive oil."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Zaalouk is watery",
              "cause": "Aubergine released too much moisture or not reduced long enough",
              "fix": "Cook uncovered over medium heat, stirring often, until the mixture thickens and holds on a spoon."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshooterItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Aubergine is still fibrous",
              "cause": "Not cooked long enough",
              "fix": "Cover and continue cooking on low for another 10 minutes. The aubergine should be completely collapsed before mashing."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Zaalouk appears across Morocco as a starter and as part of the array of small salads that begin a formal Moroccan meal. It is closely related to the Tunisian slata mechouia, which is made from roasted peppers and tomatoes, and to the Turkish imam bayildi. A similar courgette version exists in Morocco called courgette zaalouk. The dish is excellent served on khobz (Moroccan bread) or as a side to grilled meat."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
